      "rationale": "The query calls for grouping by priority, but an original 'priority' column already exists; this is largely redundant with it, offering only a normalized numeric restatement. Values (1-4) are soundly derived from the source priority."
    },
    {
      "name": "category_priority",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Combining category and priority into a single key directly supports the query's two-way breakdown of duration across category and priority, enabling grouped comparison. Composite values match the source category and priority fields."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
  "source_groundedness": 0.92,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively give strong analytical leverage for the query: duration is the target measure and category_priority provides the exact grouping cross-tab needed. duration_minutes and priority_level are weaker, being restatements/redundancies of duration_seconds and the existing priority column respectively. All values are well grounded in the timestamp, category, and priority information present in the table, with no observed hallucination; silent-row behaviour is not an issue here."
